<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spearthrower Owl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 439</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Jatz'om Kuy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spearthrower Owl is the name given by scholars to a powerful lord named in Maya inscriptions as the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yax-nuun-ayiin-i">Yax Nuun Ayiin I</a>, who became king of Tikal in 379 after the arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyaj-kak">Siyaj K'ak'</a>. His name glyph combines an owl and a spear-thrower, emblems associated with Teotihuacan, and many scholars think he was a ruler of Teotihuacan itself. The inscriptions record his death in 439.</p></div>
